Z||000000||AusFiero||09-24-2001||07:53 AM||||Well I have knocked a guy down on price ona Fiero and am now in 2 minds as to which car to buy. I have the 86 SE at $11,000 or a t-topped 86 4cylinder auto with an SE body for $7,000.<P>So how hard is it to use all my old 86 V6 5 speed GT stuff in the 4 cylinder car?<P>Do I have to use the whole harness?<BR>I know I need a new radiator etc.<BR>Is the brakes the same?<BR>Any other mods?<BR>How much to buy an auto box out of a V6 as an auto would be prefered anyway?<BR>What would you do take the cheaper car and modify with all the parts available or jsut start with another v6 car, which is a 4 speed by the way so I would be changing gearboxes anyway.?<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||5
Z||000001||8Ball||09-24-2001||08:44 AM||||Me personally I would buy the 4 cyl ttop and put the v6 stuff in it. I am not certain but I think you would have to swap the computer and harness with the motor as well. But worth the money you will save. And you will have another t-top.||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||09-24-2001||08:59 AM||||Are you sure the 4 cyl just has the SE body? I mean, is it put on with sheet metal screws or something? Reason I ask is that GM did make SE 4 cyl cars, but a very small amount (1400 or so) . I'd think that an 86 SE 4 cyl with a t-top would be a very rare bird indeed. If it's not a real SE and the body pieces were tacked on a basic 2M4, I'd shy away from it. (Can you putt nitrus on an 4cyl?)||||reg||1
Z||000003||AusFiero||09-24-2001||09:06 AM||||Hmmm interesting stimpy. It has SE gauges and such. I just assumed it was tacked on. Owner swears it was always like that. Don't tell me I have stumbled on a rare one. I want a custom Fiero this time around. Not one I would feel obliged to keep stock  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cozmo||09-24-2001||09:14 AM||||Sounds like the 4 cyl. T-top is a better match, as you have a donor car for all the V-6 stuff (almost) and you'd have some extra $$$.<BR>Auto trannys and brake parts are the same any model until '88, so you should have no problems mixing and matching.  Like 8ball said, you will need a rear V-6 auto wiring harness and computer to make it all work. Also a V-6 auto radiator.<BR>The nice thing about doing an engine swap is you get to clean and detail the whole engine bay...With all the great body mods you do, that would really set it off!<BR>Good luck and I look forward to seeing what you do with THIS one!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>If stimpy is right, it may be rare enough to keep stock... <P>BobC||||reg||1
Z||000005||NEPTUNE||09-24-2001||09:38 AM||||I believe the v6 fuel pump is different, too. <BR>My 2 cents? go with the SE||||reg||1
Z||000006||gargoyle||09-24-2001||10:10 AM||||Aus, I vote for the 86 t-top. You already have a V6 for and like someone said, you'll be  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> $4000 ahead  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. If you wanted to mod the engine that would be a nice starting spot.  Repeat after me t-top t-top t-top.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||FieroBUZZ||09-24-2001||11:21 AM||||I vote for the T-top.  It sounded like you were going to modify the drivetrain anyways. The 4k extra will help.  It may be time to try to shoehorn something exotic from the land of Oz into the beast.  You have the rear clip/wireloom/fueltank etc. from the wreck.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/bzzsiggy_2.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000008||FieroMaster88||09-24-2001||12:17 PM||||Well Aus, If you go with the 86 T-Top it would not be that hard to swap engines.  You already have the V6, wire harness, computer and all.  The engine wire haired comes through the left side of the firewall, and all the interior wire harness is already set up for the V6.  You do need to switch the fuel pump.  The 4 cyl with Throttle body injection uses somewhere in the neighborhood of 14PSI, the MPFI V6 uses 45 psi.  You could take the fuel pump out of your GT. <P>The trans swap is not hard either.  You already have everything you need.  You take the automatic trans cooler lines off, run the metal hydraulic clutch line, mount the pedals, install the master cylinder and slave cylinder.  That is that.<P>You do need to switch the throttle cable too.  The 4 cyl throttle cable is different (longer I believe, cant remember) than the 6 cyl cable.  <P>So I would say, seeing how you have a donor car for the engine, trans and wiring harness and the 86 SE is cheaper (and has T-Tops) you should get it and swap in your V6.  Sounds like a really nice deal! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jamessig.jpg">              <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>Not your ordinary 88 coupe!||||reg||1
Z||000009||Phil||09-24-2001||12:35 PM||||One thing to consider on the ttop - there just about NO replacement parts- if the seals and moldings are in sad shape I'd pass on it||||reg||1
Z||000010||Formula||09-24-2001||01:18 PM||||would you feel more compfortable switching an engine or a t-top.  No cutting in the engine but its a lot of work.  A lot of cutting and welding in the t-top but you are the almighty body man!<P>but if you swap motors youd save $4k, for that you could have a quad 4 fastback!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Formulasigs.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||AusFiero||09-24-2001||03:43 PM||||Starting to confirn what I have been thinking. A couple of things. The t-tops don't leak the owner tells me. But either way I still have the t-tops in my old GT which don't leak and also have a brand new set of t-top rubbers never fitted. So that would give me 4 glass tops and 3 complete sets of rubbers. That would almost make me greedy wouldn't it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> If it doesn't leak I may be persuaded to sell 1 set of rubbers. NOT the new ones.<P>Now to the auto. I really would prefer an automatic car so are they really the same in the 4 and 6 cylinder models? If so I will need to get a new flywheel, a V6 auto radiator, a new engine harness off and an ECM of a 86 auto 6 cylinder car. No biggie but is everything else the same? How well do these autos handle power considering I am going to turbo the beast? Sorry for so many questions but I need to work all this out in the next 48 hours before I fly down to Melbourne to pick up one of the cars.<P>This is just another idea again. One with heaps of work and more a fantasy as I don't think I could handle the work involved. Get the 4 cylinder auto car. Buy a damaged Subaru WRX turbo I have found for the same price and make the worlds first front engined all wheel drive Fiero. Yeah I know the front engined thing has been done before but all wheel drive sounds intersting for a Fiero  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Leper||09-24-2001||03:49 PM||||I guess it coms down to weather you want a cheaper t-top car, or pay more for a car without t-tops but with a lot of other upgrades. (If I remember the other threads correctly.) With your GT, you have almost enough parts to make either car the same body and drivetrain wise. So you just have to decide where you want to place your efforts. ||||reg||1
Z||000013||beer_stud_21||09-24-2001||07:05 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Get the 4 cylinder auto car. Buy a damaged Subaru WRX turbo I have found for the same price and make the worlds first front engined all wheel drive Fiero. Yeah I know the front engined thing has been done before but all wheel drive sounds intersting for a Fiero  <HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Now that would be a <B>BEAST!</B>  A 3800SC in the back and a WRX turbo in the front.  Better make at least one of them an auto tho.  It would be a royal PITA to shift two engines... LOL.  I say get the T-top and swap a 3800SC or turbo a quad 4.  OR get one of your exotic Austrailian engines, like that rover v8 you were showing us and put that in there.  <P>-Marlin<p>[This message has been edited by beer_stud_21 (edited 09-24-2001).]||||reg||1
